stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Active: Admin: POST /api/v1/authorities<br/>→ INSERT authorities (id, name, country_code, subsets, is_active=TRUE)

    Active --> Active: Admin: PUT /api/v1/authorities/{id}<br/>→ INSERT new authorities row sharing the same id<br/>(updated name, subsets, description)

    Active --> Inactive: Admin: DELETE /api/v1/authorities/{id}<br/>→ INSERT new authorities row with is_active=FALSE

    Inactive --> Active: Admin: POST again<br/>→ INSERT new row with is_active=TRUE

    note right of Active
        Latest authorities row has is_active=TRUE.
        - Authority users can search via GET /v1/identifiers/{id}
        - Authority users can request datasets via GET /v1/dataset/...
        - subsets[] field controls eFTI subsets users may request
        - Each authority user's own subsets must be ⊆ authorities.subsets
        - Authority users can send POST /v1/follow-up/...
    end note

    note right of Inactive
        Latest authorities row has is_active=FALSE.
        - Latest-row lookup excludes this authority
          (filter is_active=TRUE)
        - All authority users get 401 on next request
        - Historical access logs retained in audit_log (GDPR Art 30)
        - Old authorities rows archived nightly by CronManager (Epic 26)
    end note
